<p class="lead">We collect as little as we need to run the site. This page explains what that is and what we do with it.</p>

<h2>What we collect</h2>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Account details:</strong> your name, email address, department, optional student ID, and your password stored only as a secure hash. We cannot read your password.</li>
  <li><strong>Your uploads:</strong> the files you upload and details you enter (title, course, type, semester, description), plus the upload time and download counts.</li>
  <li><strong>Reports:</strong> reports you submit about files.</li>
</ul>

<h2>How we use it</h2>
<ul>
  <li>To let you sign in, upload, download and manage your files</li>
  <li>To review uploads and handle reports and takedown requests</li>
  <li>To keep the site secure and prevent abuse</li>
</ul>
<p>We do not sell your data, show ads or run advertising trackers.</p>

<h2>What other people can see</h2>
<ul>
  <li>Your name appears next to files you upload.</li>
  <li>Your email address, student ID and department are visible only to site administrators.</li>
</ul>

<h2>Cookies and browser storage</h2>
<ul>
  <li>A <strong>session cookie</strong> keeps you signed in. It is needed for the site to work.</li>
  <li>Your <strong>day or night mode</strong> choice is saved in your browser's local storage so the site remembers it.</li>
  <li>Page fonts load from Google Fonts, which receives your IP address and browser details when your browser fetches them.</li>
</ul>

<h2>How long we keep data</h2>
<p>We keep your account and uploads until you ask us to delete them. You can delete your own uploads from the site at any time.</p>

<h2>Security</h2>
<p>Passwords are hashed, forms are protected against forged requests, and uploaded files are checked before they are accepted. No website can promise perfect security, so please use a password you do not use elsewhere.</p>

<h2>Your choices</h2>
<p>You can ask us to correct or delete your account and data, or to remove files you uploaded. See the <a href="/contact">contact page</a>.</p>

<h2>Changes</h2>
<p>If we change this policy we will update the date at the top of the page.</p>
